+            <option value="staff">Staff: answers customers and handles approvals</option>
+            <option value="admin">Admin: also changes settings, prices and connections</option>
+          </select>
+        </label>
+        <label className="field">Expires
+          <select value={expiry} onChange={(e) => setExpiry(e.target.value)}>{EXPIRY.map(([v, l]) => <option key={v} value={v}>{l}</option>)}</select>
+        </label>
+        <div><button className="btn primary" disabled={busy || !tenant}>{busy ? "Generating…" : "Generate token"}</button></div>
+      </form>
+      <details>
+        <summary className="small" style={{ cursor: "pointer", fontWeight: 650 }}>Security practices for tokens</summary>
+        <ul className="small stack" style={{ marginTop: "0.6rem", paddingLeft: "1.1rem", gap: "0.35rem" }}>
+          <li><strong>Send it privately, once.</strong> Give it to the person directly (in person, or a private message that disappears). Never post it in a group chat, email thread, ticket or screenshot.</li>
+          <li><strong>One token per person.</strong> When someone leaves, revoke only theirs. Shared tokens mean you can&apos;t tell who did what.</li>
+          <li><strong>Give the least access.</strong> Use Staff unless they must change prices, settings or connections. Few people should be Admin.</li>
+          <li><strong>Let tokens expire.</strong> The default is 90 days. Generate a new one before the old one ends, then revoke the old one. Use &ldquo;never expires&rdquo; only for a system you can&apos;t re-key.</li>
+          <li><strong>Revoke at once if exposed.</strong> If a token was pasted somewhere it shouldn&apos;t be, or a phone or laptop was lost, revoke it on the business&apos;s page and issue a new one. Revoking takes effect on the next request.</li>
+          <li><strong>We can&apos;t show it again.</strong> Only a one-way hash is stored. If it&apos;s lost, generate a new one rather than hunting for the old one.</li>
+          <li><strong>Check &ldquo;Last used&rdquo; now and then.</strong> A token nobody uses, or one used at odd times, should be revoked. Every issue and revoke is written to the audit log.</li>
+          <li><strong>Keep platform keys apart.</strong> A platform key (this dashboard) can reach every business. Keep few of them, never give one to a business, and never put a token in code, a repository or a browser&apos;s saved notes.</li>
+        </ul>
+      </details>
+    </section>
